  <data name="Exp_Searching" xml:space="preserve"><value>Looking for a router (UPnP) …</value></data>
  <data name="Exp_NoneActive" xml:space="preserve"><value>✓  No port forwardings active</value></data>
  <data name="Exp_NoneActive_Detail" xml:space="preserve"><value>The router reports no open forwardings into the LAN. Note that vendor cloud or P2P access bypasses UPnP and would not show up here — check that in the camera app itself.</value></data>
  <data name="Exp_NoRouter" xml:space="preserve"><value>No UPnP router found</value></data>
  <data name="Exp_NoRouter_Detail" xml:space="preserve"><value>The router does not answer UPnP — often UPnP is simply switched off, which is good for security. Check port forwardings in the router menu instead. You can still look up the public IP above on Shodan.</value></data>
